@
message TREES_MSG
THE TREES OF THE FOREST ARE LARGE HARDWOOD OAK AND MAPLE,\n
WITH AN OCCASIONAL GROVE OF PINE OR SPRUCE.\n
THERE IS QUITE A BIT OF UNDER-GROWTH, LARGELY BIRCH AND\n
ASH SAPLINGS PLUS NONDESCRIPT BUSHES OF VARIOUS SORTS.\n
THIS TIME OF YEAR VISIBILITY IS QUITE RESTRICTED BY\n
ALL THE LEAVES, BUT TRAVEL IS QUITE EASY IF YOU DETOUR AROUND THE\n
SPRUCE AND BERRY BUSHES.
@
message DIG_MSG
DIGGING WITHOUT A SHOVEL IS QUITE IMPRACTICAL.\n
EVEN WITH A SHOVEL PROGRESS IS UNLIKELY.
@
message LOST_MSG
I'M AS CONFUSED AS YOU ARE.
@
message MIST_MSG
MIST IS A WHITE VAPOR, USUALLY WATER, SEEN FROM TIME TO TIME IN CAVERNS.\n
IT CAN BE FOUND ANYWHERE BUT IS FREQUENTLY A SIGN OF A DEEP PIT\n
LEADING DOWN TO WATER.
@
message WATCH_IT
WATCH IT!
@
message STOP_MSG
I DON'T KNOW THE WORD "STOP".  USE "QUIT" IF YOU WANT TO GIVE UP.
@
message SWIM_MSG
I DON'T KNOW HOW.
@
message WET_FEET
YOUR FEET ARE NOW WET.
@
message WHERE_MSG
WHERE?
@
message FOO_START_OVER
WHAT'S THE MATTER, CAN'T YOU READ?  NOW YOU'D BEST START OVER.
@
message EGGS_VANISH
